<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal authorises euro-denominated loan.</title>
<headline>Portugal authorises euro-denominated loan.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government authorised the Institute of Management of Public Credit (IGCP) to issue a 10-year loan in escudos for up to 50 billion escudos that can be automatically re-denominated in euros at the launch of Economic and Monetary Union (EMU), the Finance Ministry said.</p>
<p>The loans are called &quot;Treasury Bonds-OT-Euro,&quot; a statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The financing of the state is taking into consideration the launch of EMU, reflecting Portugal's commitment to participate in the first stage of EMU,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
